From: Try Omarchy contributors
Subject: [PATCH] audio/sdl: open the recording device off the BQL

What: the SDL backend opens, switches and closes the recording device on a
thread of its own. The guest's enable/disable only tells that thread. Until
the device runs, or when it cannot be opened, the voice gives the guest
silence at the stream's rate (run_buffer_in), so the capture stream keeps
going; a device that opens late is used if the guest still records. After
5 s without a device, one warning in the log.

Why: on macOS, SDL's recording open ends in AudioQueueStart, which waits for
coreaudiod. That can take minutes (a pending microphone permission, a slow
device): sample showed it under intel_hda_set_st_ctl on a vCPU thread
holding the BQL, so the whole VM stopped for about four minutes, then the
open failed with 268451843 (MACH_RCV_TIMED_OUT). Now only the capture
thread waits.

sdl2-compat runs every SDL_OpenAudioDevice() under one global lock, so a
playback open under the BQL would wait behind a slow recording open. Opens
now take sdl_open_lock: the capture thread waits for it, playback opens under
the BQL only try it and retry on the next audio tick (playback starts a
little later instead of the VM stopping).

Applies after qemu-sdl-audio-device-selection.patch and
qemu-hda-full-ring-recovery.patch.

Upstream: upstreamable in spirit (the SDL backend opens devices under the
BQL), but it builds on the try-omarchy route patch; not sent.

Tested in OmacVM: OmacVM.app signed with the Developer ID, a fresh VM and an existing
one: pw-record 5 s gives sound (not zeros) while SSH from the Mac and the
guest's ping to 10.0.2.2 keep answering (no gap over 0.3 s); playback and the
camera as before; 25 quick start/stops of pw-record.
Tests/audio/slow-capture-start.c holds AudioQueueStart back 20 s (silence,
then sound; pw-play waits for it), fails it (silence and the error, the VM
runs), and the VM powers off within seconds while a start is held.

Adapted from OmacVM's patch of the same name (MIT,
https://github.com/gillesgoetsch/OmacVM), with its log lines and
environment variable renamed for Try Omarchy.

